# Reverse proxy + automatic HTTPS for the shared-platform model (one
# domain, every hospital on a subdomain of it -- see "Shared-platform
# tenant resolution" in CLAUDE.md).
#
# A true wildcard TLS certificate (*.ROOT_DOMAIN) needs a DNS-01 challenge,
# which needs a Caddy build with a DNS-provider plugin baked in for
# whichever registrar/DNS host you end up using. On-demand TLS sidesteps
# that entirely: Caddy issues a normal per-hostname certificate via HTTP-01
# the first time each subdomain is actually visited, using the stock Caddy
# image, no provider-specific plugin or API token required. New hospital
# onboarded -> point its subdomain's DNS at this server -> first visit
# gets a real cert automatically, no manual step here.
#
# The `ask` endpoint (src/app/api/internal/tls-ask) is required, not
# optional, alongside on-demand TLS: without it, the wildcard DNS record
# pointing every possible subdomain at this server means anyone could type
# a random subdomain and make this box request a real Let's Encrypt
# certificate for it -- wasteful, and a way to burn through Let's Encrypt's
# rate limit. The ask endpoint only approves hostnames that are either the
# bare root domain or a real, active hospital's subdomain.

{
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://app:3000/api/internal/tls-ask
	}
}

{$ROOT_DOMAIN}, *.{$ROOT_DOMAIN} {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}

	reverse_proxy app:3000
}
